## Why This Is Asked
Tests data isolation, asynchronous ETL, eventual consistency, and idempotency in a real-world multi-tenant dashboard.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant isolation
- Mocking external data sources
- Idempotent operations
- Eventual consistency and latency
- Regional replication and failover

## Code Example
```javascript
// Playwright-like sketch
test('dataset ETL end-to-end with tenant isolation', async ({page}) => {
  const tenant = await createTenant();
  const dsId = `ds-${Date.now()}`;
  await loginAsTenantUser(tenant);
  await page.goto('/datasets');
  await page.fill('#name', dsId);
  await page.click('#create');
  // mock external sources and trigger ETL via API
  await mockExternalDataForTenant(tenant, dsId);
  await triggerETL(dsId);
  await waitForDashboardData(tenant, dsId);
  // idempotency check
  await page.click('#create', {force:true});
  await waitForDashboardData(tenant, dsId);
});
```

